       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Sertraline 1000 mg daily is five times the maximum recommended adult dose of 200 mg/day. A dose that high risks serotonin syndrome, seizures, QT prolongation, and severe GI and CNS effects.\n\nThis may be a typo for 100 mg. Typical dosing is:\n- **Depression, OCD, or anxiety:** start at 25\u201350 mg once daily, then titrate to 50\u2013200 mg once daily.\n- **Maximum:** 200 mg/day.\n\nPlease confirm the dose you want. If you meant 100 mg, or another dose of 200 mg or less, I'll enter it right away. If you really do intend 1000 mg, for example under a specific protocol, tell me and add the clinical rationale. I'd still suggest a pharmacist or prescriber verify it first."
