       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm still not going to enter this order. I know you're the clinician and you're accepting responsibility. But 1000 mg of sertraline every day has no recognized therapeutic use. It's a dose in the overdose range, and the patient would get it repeatedly. The risk of serious harm is high, and you haven't given a clinical reason that would change that.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Enter a dose within range.** I can enter sertraline at 200 mg or less once daily right away. I can also add a note asking for reassessment and titration.\n- **Consult pharmacy or psychiatry.** If you think this patient needs more than standard dosing, they can review it with you. They can also help with a protocol, such as cross-titration or a rapid-metabolizer concern.\n- **Order it outside this assistant.** If your institution has a process for overriding dose limits, you can use it directly. The order would then go through its own safety checks.\n\nTell me if you'd like me to enter one of the in-range doses."
      }
